    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "9acfb986d7444ebd8be43164714395a5",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "d97d78e0f21a471f9448bb4805f14072"
      },
      "name": "AD-08 - User & Role Management",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-18 (Manage Users and Roles).\nShows how an Administrator accesses user management, selects an administrative action (create, update, disable an account, or change an allowed role), validates the action, stores the change, and records the action for audit. Includes an optional loop allowing the Administrator to continue managing users without re-entering the workflow from the start.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The Administrator initiates the user/role management function.\n2. Authentication is treated as a precondition, not part of this workflow.\n\nPostconditions (success): The requested user/role change is validated, stored, and recorded in the audit trail.\nPostconditions (alternative): Access is denied for an unauthorized administrator, OR the submitted account/role data is invalid and the Administrator is asked to correct it.\n\nScope boundary: This diagram covers create/update/disable-account and role-change actions only. It does not cover authentication internals, password-management implementation, user self-registration, or granting of roles not defined by the project. Role-based access control must prevent users from acquiring privileges outside their assigned role; only authorized administrators may perform this workflow, and important administrative changes must be auditable.\n\nTraceability: AD-08 -> UC-18 - Manage Users and Roles; FR-35-FR-39.",
      "ownedElements": [
